---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import DocCallout from "../../components/docs/DocCallout.astro";
import DocCode from "../../components/docs/DocCode.astro";

const toc = [
  { title: "Host CLI", href: "#host-cli", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Pairing & Auth", href: "#pairing-auth", depth: 2 },
  { title: "App Capabilities", href: "#app-capabilities", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Notifications & Live Activities", href: "#notifications-live", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Tophat", href: "#tophat", depth: 2 },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Mobile"
  subtitle="Host-side mobile commands in packages/nikcli and the Expo app in packages/mobile."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="host-cli" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Host CLI</h2>
    <p>
      Mobile starts from the host machine. <code>nikcli mobile</code> serves the pairing and mobile
      API surface, while <code>nikcli mobile tophat</code> helps push builds onto devices or simulators.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash">
      nikcli mobile serve --pair
      nikcli mobile token list
      nikcli mobile token revoke
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="pairing-auth" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Pairing & Auth</h2>
    <p>
      Mobile has three distinct auth layers: host pairing via bearer tokens, in-app user login, and
      GitHub authentication for repo import and PR workflows.
    </p>
    <DocCallout type="info" title="Public exposure">
      <p>
        Public mobile servers should require additional protection such as basic auth instead of
        exposing a raw host endpoint.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="app-capabilities" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>App Capabilities</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Area</th>
          <th>What ships today</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Sessions</td><td>Realtime SSE streaming, plan/code composer modes, slash suggestions, and command palette actions.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Approvals</td><td>Permission prompts and question responses rendered directly in the app.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Tool output</td><td>Dedicated tool call cards, attachment previews, and message history.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>GitHub</td><td>Repo import, worktree creation, publish PR, cleanup, status, diff, stage, and commit flows.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Settings</td><td>Providers, connectors, MCP, skills, agents, commands, memories, tokens, GitHub, and plugin settings.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Offline</td><td>Queued send retry when the app returns to the foreground.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="notifications-live" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Notifications & Live Activities</h2>
    <p>
      The app supports local notifications and iOS Live Activities for session readiness, approval
      requests, and other foreground-worthy state changes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="tophat" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Tophat</h2>
    <p>
      Tophat support is configurable under <code>config.mobile.tophat</code> and lets nikcli install
      local or remote mobile build artifacts on iOS and Android targets.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
